    <item>
      <title>Building ChoCo 🛠️</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/building/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/building/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This page covers the &lt;strong&gt;hardware build&lt;/strong&gt; of ChoCo, from PCB to a fully assembled controller.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ChoCo is designed to be easy to build using standard components and simple soldering tools.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;What you need&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;what-you-need&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#what-you-need&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Required tools&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;required-tools&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#required-tools&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Soldering iron (fine tip recommended)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Solder (lead-free or leaded)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Multimeter (optional, but useful)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Main components&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;main-components&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#main-components&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RP2040 board&lt;/strong&gt; (Raspberry Pi Pico or compatible)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3×4 keypad matrix&lt;/strong&gt; (7 keys used)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analog joystick module&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OLED display&lt;/strong&gt; (SSD1306, 128×64, I2C)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Passive components (resistors, capacitors)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Headers / connectors as specified in the BOM&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A full &lt;strong&gt;Bill of Materials (BOM)&lt;/strong&gt; with exact part numbers is available in the repository.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Flashing &amp; Debugging ⚡</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/flashing_debugging/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/flashing_debugging/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This page explains how to &lt;strong&gt;build, upload, and debug&lt;/strong&gt; the ChoCo firmware using PlatformIO.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;PlatformIO is the recommended workflow and provides an easy setup for RP2040 boards.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Recommended setup&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;recommended-setup&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#recommended-setup&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VS Code&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PlatformIO extension&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Raspberry Pi Pico (or compatible RP2040 board)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Build &amp;amp; upload (PlatformIO)&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;build--upload-platformio&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#build--upload-platformio&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;VS Code (recommended)&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;vs-code-recommended&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#vs-code-recommended&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Install the &lt;strong&gt;PlatformIO&lt;/strong&gt; extension&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Open the &lt;code&gt;ChoCo&lt;/code&gt; project folder&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Click:&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✔️ &lt;strong&gt;Build&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;➡️ &lt;strong&gt;Upload&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;🔌 &lt;strong&gt;Monitor&lt;/strong&gt; (to view logs)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;CLI (optional)&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;cli-optional&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#cli-optional&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight-wrapper&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;pio run&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;pio run -t upload&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;pio device monitor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Getting Started 🚀</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/getting_started/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/getting_started/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Getting started with &lt;strong&gt;ChoCo&lt;/strong&gt; is simple.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;ChoCo is an open-hardware USB-MIDI controller, designed to be built using standard PCB manufacturing and easy-to-source components.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This guide walks you through the basic steps needed to go from files to a working device.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;1. Download the PCB files&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;1-download-the-pcb-files&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#1-download-the-pcb-files&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Start by downloading the &lt;strong&gt;Gerber files&lt;/strong&gt;, which are ready for PCB manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
